 "N174": {"text":"Scheibe, R. R. (2002) An Overview of Studded and Studless Tire Traction and Safety, WA-RD 551.1, Washington State Transportation Center for WSDOT/FHWA, Table 4 (data of Nordstrom & Samuelsson, VTI): Studded tyres on smooth ice at -1 to -14 C: friction 0.14-0.26 (optimum slip), 0.12-0.19 (locked wheel); 0.18-0.27 on stud-roughened ice. Ichihara report not found","opened":true},
 "N175": {"text":"Hsu, J., Shaw, R., Novak, A., Li, Y., Ormerod, M., Newton, R., Dutta, T. & Fernie, G. (2016) Slip resistance of winter footwear on snow and ice measured using maximum achievable incline, Ergonomics 59(5):717-728, doi:10.1080/00140139.2015.1084051: Bench COF 0.08 wet ice, 0.20 dry ice, averaged over six winter boot styles (not 'bare boots')","opened":true},
 "N176": {"text":"Design: Mid's soldiers (02-rules-units.js UNIT, spear to treb; 04-rules-tech.js the barracks, range, stable, smith and siege lines and their tiers; 06-rules-tuning.js TEACH_TO; 08-core.js stats, armyOf, BUSY, armyFree, armyRoom, clsMax, armyFull; 01-rules-basics.js POPMAX, ARMYMAX, BNSIZE; 39-huddle.js kindOf; 18-figures.js KIT, person, ELITE_LOOK, elitePennant, sprite, elephant and the looks) by Albert's call, Nov 5 10:26: the Unit shell, each kind its settings (age, class, level, look, speed, health); health and damage open for his play test","opened":true,"kind":"design"},
 "N177": {"text":"Asian elephant: San Diego Zoo Wildlife Alliance factsheet; arrows/bolts/guns: Williams, 'What can scientific analysis tell us about the effectiveness of medieval arms and armour' (citing Bergman et al. 1988; Krenn 1990); sword: HEMA Penzance (2026): Male Asian elephant ~3,600 kg avg (to 6,000), 2.7 m shoulder; crossbow (90 lb) bolt 62 m/s, ~100 g; matchlock arquebus muzzle 449 m/s; arming sword 0.9-1.3 kg. Javelin 20 m/s not found","opened":true},
 "N178": {"text":"Gao, Abeysekera, Hirvonen & Aschan (2003), The effect of footwear sole abrasion on the coefficient of friction on melting and hard ice, Int. J. Industrial Ergonomics 31(5) 323–330: kinetic friction on melting ice 0.055, on hard ice 0.18 (new soles) to 0.244 (abraded)","opened":true},
 "N179": {"text":"Burnfield & Powers (2004), Prediction of slip events during walking: an analysis of utilized coefficient of friction and available slip resistance, AAFS C52: the peak utilized friction of walking 0.21 ± 0.04 (38 people, 96.6 m/min); a slip is likely when the friction used exceeds what the floor offers","opened":true},
 "N180": {"text":"US National Weather Service glossary, blizzard (forecast.weather.gov/glossary.php?word=bliz; weather.gov/dtx/winter_defs): sustained wind or frequent gusts to 35 mph or more, and falling or blowing snow reducing visibility frequently below 1/4 mile, for 3 hours or longer","opened":true},
 "N181": {"text":"Pugh, L. G. C. E. (1971) The influence of wind resistance in running and walking and the mechanical efficiency of work against horizontal or vertical forces, J. Physiol. 213(2):255-276, doi:10.1113/jphysiol.1971.sp009381: O2 uptake rises with wind velocity squared; work against wind more efficient than against gravity. CdA 0.45 m2 not in the abstract (full text blocked)","opened":false},
 "N182": {"text":"Seliga, Hazen & Burnley, nowcasting snowfall rate from visibility (AMS paper 104640): S = c σ, c from about 0.6 early in an event to 0.2 late (0.16–0.31 in its cases); with Rasmussen, Vivekanandan, Cole, Myers & Masters (1999), J. Appl. Meteor.: the relation varies with the snow's type up to tenfold; the rate read as mm/h of water, to confirm","opened":true},
 "N183": {"text":"Atlas, D. (1953) Optical extinction by rainfall, J. Meteorology 10:486-488, as given in Mulvey, G. J. (1973) The investigation of snowfall rate using optical techniques, M.S. thesis, SUNY Albany: V = 9.3 R^-0.67 km (theory, Marshall-Palmer drops), so sigma = 3.912/V = 0.42 R^0.67 per km; empirical (Bergeron rain) V = 11.6 R^-0.63, so sigma = 0.34 R^0.63","opened":true},
 "N184": {"text":"Harper, B. A., Kepert, J. D. & Ginger, J. D. (2010) Guidelines for converting between various wind averaging periods in tropical cyclone conditions, WMO/TD-No. 1555 (factors from the 2008 AMS draft, paper 4B.1): 3-s gust / 10-min mean: off-land 1.52, in-land 1.66; 1.42-1.44 against a 2-3 min mean","opened":true},
 "N185": {"text":"Design: Albert, Nov 5 18:07–18:08: pace by the floor, the weather, mass and gravity, never by the calendar (Pandolf); the effects law, boosts add once, cuts one at a time on what is left, never 0 or 100%; weather one system by an intensity from the dice, the blizzard by the NWS; grip by measured friction; crampons for foot and haulers, horses wait for horseshoes; weather visuals by code and math (SoRen's)","opened":true,"kind":"design"},
 "N186": {"text":"Rain classes per MANOBS via Barani Design; Beaufort scale (Wikipedia): Violent rain >50 mm/h (MANOBS, not shown as Met Office); Beaufort 8 gale 17.2-20.7 m/s. Snow 5 mm/h water not found","opened":true},
 "N187": {"text":"Locatelli, J. D. & Hobbs, P. V. (1974) Fall speeds and masses of solid precipitation particles, J. Geophys. Res. 79(15):2185-2197: Unrimed dendrite aggregates 1-14 mm fall 0.5-1.4 m/s","opened":true},
 "N188": {"text":"Design: Mid's blow, nerve, a soldier's day, squads, formations and muster (16-sim-fight.js fromWhere, hurt, plunder, plunderBld; 14-sim-troops.js solTick, routSecs, nearHome, shot; 08-core.js nearestFoe, foeValue, GROUP_R, groupPower, canBeat, bestFoe, nearestFoeBld, vsMul, rangeFrom, rangeOf, kiteOf, orderSet, selName, hasCmd, formOf, marching, shapeOf, dialOf, cycle, temperOf, clsOf, rebattalion; 12-sim-core.js died, formUp; 13-sim-civil.js homeSpot; 11-orders.js musterN, musterCost, musterWhy, muster; 28-army-quick.js forming, drillOn, dress, drillHold, musterGap; 39-huddle.js sqPlan, sqUnits, sqOut, INTENT; 23-view-things.js sparkDraw, drawStandards; 24-view-overlays.js drawTracers; 37-events.js wearMul; 09-nav.js findBlocker; 06-rules-tuning.js MORALE, FLANKING, FLANK, YARD, KITE, GARRISON, FORM, COLUMN, TEMPER, GRID, FORMING, CHOKE; 01-rules-basics.js BN, BNSIZE, PLUNDER, RICH; 04-rules-tech.js the Walls, Towers, Garrison and Command lines)","opened":true,"kind":"design"},
 "N189": {"text":"Park, J. L. (2011) Arrow behaviour in free flight, Proc. IMechE Part P: J. Sports Eng. Tech. 225(4):241-252, doi:10.1177/1754337111398542: Citation confirmed; Cd values not in any opened page (full text blocked; Park et al. 2013 points to Olsen 1967)","opened":false},
 "N190": {"text":"Design: Mid's finger, orders, missions and the War Director (26-input.js hitAt, tapAt, picked, setPick, pickToggle, order, boxPick, ordAt, HOLD_MS, PRESS_SHOW, DBL_MS; 11-orders.js centreOf, routeK, etaOf, march, ordersTick; 39-huddle.js HUD, missionsTick, reinforcePlan, waveLine, hudFire, hudGo, aimSpot, aimColor, drawReticle; 28-army-quick.js sendable, armyStatus, ARMY_STILL, free, freeWhy, showQuick, quickGo, chokeAt, coverNear, ambushAt, DIRECTS, DIRECT_OF, direct; 36-economy.js charge, fallBack; 14-sim-troops.js ambushTick; 17-ai.js gapOnRoad, chokeClaim; 06-rules-tuning.js DIRECT, CHOKE, AMBUSH, CHARGE, FALLBACK; 23-view-things.js drawTouch, drawOrders, flagAt, leavesOver), read in staging and mid/src for F21+F22","opened":true},
